.TH SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_ENHANCED_REPORTS 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_ENHANCED_REPORTS \- A variable controlling whether enhanced reports should be used for controllers when using the HIDAPI driver.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_ENHANCED_REPORTS \(dqSDL_JOYSTICK_ENHANCED_REPORTS\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enhanced reports allow rumble and effects on Bluetooth PlayStation controllers and gyro on Nintendo Switch controllers, but break Windows DirectInput for other applications that don\(aqt use SDL\[char46]
.PP
Once enhanced reports are enabled, they can\(aqt be disabled on PlayStation controllers without power cycling the controller\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: enhanced reports are not enabled\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: enhanced reports are enabled\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dqauto\(dq: enhanced features are advertised to the application, but SDL doesn\(aqt change the controller report mode unless the application uses them\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be enabled anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

